cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use claim-check in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "claim-check"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/claim-check"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/claim-check"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Every number you publish is a claim. claim-check binds each figure in a document to the
  artifact it came from (a JSON file, a log, a command's output), recomputes it on every CI
  run, and fails the build when doc and source drift apart. No LLM, no API key, no network,
  no dependencies. The verdict is an exit code. Free, MIT.
keywords:
  - continuous-integration
  - documentation
  - verification
  - github-action
  - reproducibility
